<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Hordaland</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom around the fjords of modern Bergen, remembered in saga tradition for resisting Harald Fairhair's unification of Norway.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hordaland, the coast and fjords around what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a>, was a populous district of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>. The sagas describe it as a kingdom in the 9th century, ruled by local kings with fleets and many retainers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its people farmed, fished and sailed; many western Norwegian raiders and settlers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> came from here. Hordaland belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulating">Gulating</a> law province. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> vowed not to cut his hair until he ruled all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> after Gyda, daughter of a Hordaland king, refused to marry a petty king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Its kings joined the coalition defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hafrsfjord">Hafrsfjord</a>, traditionally around 872, and Hordaland became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a>, founded in the 11th century, grew into medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway's</a> chief town.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hordaland.jpg" alt="Hordaland" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hordaland_Hardangerfjord_05.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Hordaland, Hordafylke</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=hordaland" aria-label="Hordaland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4805 161 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hordaland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5125 417L5225 425"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5125 417h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5125 417h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=hordaland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
